{"action":"revised","summary":"Fixed the single mechanical failure from the filing preflight: the abstract exceeded the 150-word limit of 37 CFR 1.72(b). The abstract is now 141 words (143 if hyphenated terms are split), while still describing the shell, suspended perforated tray, side supply and lower return passages, the spacer frame with two opposed phase-change cassettes and its openings and mating channel, the lid rib that registers the module on closing, and the passive circulation loop. No other file was changed; claims, description, numeral table, drawing descriptions, and the five figure briefs remain synchronized.","reasoning":["The only listed check was abstract length. The previous abstract measured 149 words by whitespace but 151 by a counter that splits hyphenated terms, and the draft contained two such terms (cold-chain, phase-change), which accounts exactly for the reported 151. I therefore rewrote to a length that passes under either counting method rather than trimming to exactly 150 by one measure and failing by the other.","Trimming was done by compressing phrasing and dropping one positional qualifier from the abstract (the guide ducts being beside the cassettes), not by dropping any element of the invention. Every claim-1 element still appears in the abstract: outer shell, tray on feet, lower return passage, side supply passages, spacer frame, two opposed phase-change cassettes, central inlet opening, guide ducts, peripheral outlet openings, mating channel, depending indexing rib on the lid, the registered position, the absence of a powered air mover, and the full flow loop back through tray perforations.","Substituting aligns the outlet openings with the side supply passages for in which the outlet openings overlap them keeps the abstract source-faithful, since the disclosure itself describes the peripheral outlet openings as aligned with the side supply passages. The claims and description retain the overlap wording, so claim terminology is untouched.","No drawing finding was raised, so no figure brief, numeral definition, or geometry was altered. The figure plan still distributes the 31 numerals across five focused sheets at eight or fewer per sheet, every part named in a brief is listed on that sheet, and each brief remains under the character ceiling. Verified after the edit that the abstract carries no reference numerals and that no placeholder, note, or question text exists anywhere in draft/ or figures/."],"changes":["draft/10-abstract.md: rewritten to 141 words (143 with hyphenated terms split) to satisfy 37 CFR 1.72(b), retaining every element of the independent claim and the passive circulation loop."],"prior_art_strategy":"prior_art/INDEX.md still lists no references, so the Background contains no citations and no reference is characterised anywhere in the draft. The differentiation strategy is unchanged from the drafted text: claim 1 stands on the registered passive circulation path (central rise, split along the confronting faces of two opposed cassettes, descent through guide ducts outboard of those cassettes to peripheral outlets that overlap tray-to-shell side supply passages, through tray perforations and back beneath a tray suspended on feet) combined with lid-driven registration by a depending indexing rib entering the spacer frame's mating channel, with no fan, pump, or powered air mover. The specification states the technical problems those features solve, namely an alignment that would otherwise depend on how a packer set the module down, and holding that alignment through transport vibration and inversion. This turn changed only abstract wording and did not alter claim scope, so nothing in the prior-art posture shifted. The art supplied to this draft may be incomplete and the claims should be tested against a search before filing.","questions":[],"answer":"The filing gate reported one item: the abstract was 151 words against the 150-word limit of 37 CFR 1.72(b). That is now fixed.

draft/10-abstract.md is 141 words by whitespace count and 143 if a counter splits the hyphenated terms cold-chain and phase-change, which is what produced the reported 151 previously. The shorter abstract still states the whole invention: an insulated outer shell; a product tray on feet above the shell floor leaving a lower return passage, with tray side walls spaced inward from the shell side walls forming two side supply passages; a thermal module having a rigid spacer frame holding two opposed phase-change cassettes and defining a central inlet opening, two downward guide ducts, peripheral outlet openings and a mating channel; a depending indexing rib on an insulated lid that enters the mating channel as the lid closes and shifts the module into a registered position aligning the outlet openings with the side supply passages; and, without a powered air mover, the loop in which air rises from the product region into the central inlet opening, divides along the cassette faces, descends the guide ducts and side supply passages, and returns through tray perforations to the lower return passage.

No other file was modified. The claims, detailed description, numeral table, brief description of the drawings, and all five figure briefs are unchanged and remain in step: 31 numerals each defined once and used in the description, at most eight numerals on any sheet, every part named in a brief listed on that sheet, and each brief between 2729 and 2792 characters. A sweep of draft/ and figures/ confirms no placeholder, note, question, or instruction to a person, and the abstract carries no reference numerals."}
